					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-95455#post-2811245</guid>
				<title>Stockholm Syndrome</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-95455/953-interview-a#post-2811245</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 05 May 2017 01:22:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>0cean Man</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3041060</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Hello, I am relatively new here and am unsure of the protocol related to editing articles. In light of this I would like to point out to the original author and/or anyone with the approval to edit this piece that the term &quot;Stockholm syndrome&quot; did not originate until 1973 during a bank robbery in Stockholm. This would of course bring up the issue that the interviewer would not know of this phrase as the interview apparently took place in the 1940/50s to the best of my knowledge. I would suggest a change in the date of the interview or a change in terminology to something appropriate to the time period. I apologize in advance for being so nit-picky and thank you for your time in reading this.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
